{
  "id": "CO-SB25-003-2025",
  "scope": "state:co",
  "title": "SB25-003 Semiautomatic Firearms & Rapid-Fire Devices (printed title: Concerning prohibited activity involving semiautomatic firearms)",
  "urls": [
    "https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/SB25-003",
    "https://leg.colorado.gov/bill_files/40736/download",
    "https://leg.colorado.gov/bill_votes/22096",
    "https://leg.colorado.gov/bill_votes/22181",
    "https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb25-003 and the printed act (source_url)"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "Sec. 2, 18-12-116(1)(d)(I): (d) (I) \"SPECIFIED SEMIAUTOMATIC FIREARM\" MEANS ANY OF THE FOLLOWING, EXCEPT AS PROVIDED IN SUBSECTION (1)(d)(II) OF THIS SECTION: (A) A SEMIAUTOMATIC RIFLE OR SEMIAUTOMATIC SHOTGUN WITH A DETACHABLE MAGAZINE; OR (B) A GAS-OPERATED SEMIAUTOMATIC HANDGUN WITH A DETACHABLE MAGAZINE.\nSec. 2, 18-12-116(1)(d)(II)(A)-(B): (A) A FIREARM DESIGNED TO ACCEPT, AND CAPABLE OF OPERATING ONLY WITH, .22 OR LOWER CALIBER RIMFIRE AMMUNITION, UNLESS THE FIREARM HAS A SEPARATE UPPER AND LOWER RECEIVER; (B) A FIREARM THAT IS MANUALLY OPERATED BY BOLT, PUMP, LEVER, OR SLIDE ACTION;\nSec. 2, 18-12-116(2): (2) ON OR AFTER AUGUST 1, 2026, IT IS UNLAWFUL FOR ANY PERSON TO KNOWINGLY MANUFACTURE, DISTRIBUTE, TRANSFER, SELL, OR PURCHASE A SPECIFIED SEMIAUTOMATIC FIREARM; EXCEPT THAT A PERSON MAY SELL OR TRANSFER A SPECIFIED SEMIAUTOMATIC FIREARM TO AN INDIVIDUAL RESIDING IN ANOTHER STATE OR A FEDERALLY LICENSED FIREARM DEALER.\nSec. 2, 18-12-116(5)(a)(III): (A) A BASIC FIREARMS SAFETY COURSE MUST PROVIDE A MINIMUM OF FOUR HOURS OF INSTRUCTION. (B) AN EXTENDED FIREARMS SAFETY COURSE MUST PROVIDE A MINIMUM OF TWELVE HOURS OF INSTRUCTION, WHICH MUST BE PROVIDED ON AT LEAST TWO DIFFERENT DAYS.\nSec. 2, 18-12-116(4)(b): (b) UNLAWFUL MANUFACTURE, DISTRIBUTION, TRANSFER, SALE, OR PURCHASE OF A SPECIFIED SEMIAUTOMATIC FIREARM IS A CLASS 2 MISDEMEANOR; EXCEPT THAT A SECOND OR SUBSEQUENT OFFENSE IS A CLASS 6 FELONY.\nSec. 1, 18-12-101(1)(g.7): (g.7) \"RAPID-FIRE DEVICE\" MEANS ANY DEVICE, PART, KIT, TOOL, ACCESSORY, OR COMBINATION OF PARTS THAT HAS THE EFFECT OF INCREASING THE RATE OF FIRE OF A SEMIAUTOMATIC FIREARM ABOVE THE STANDARD RATE OF FIRE FOR THE SEMIAUTOMATIC FIREARM THAT IS NOT OTHERWISE EQUIPPED WITH THAT DEVICE, PART, OR COMBINATION OF PARTS.\nSec. 8, 18-12-302(1)(a) (struck words checked on page image): (1) (a) Except as otherwise provided in this section, a person who sells, transfers, or possesses a large-capacity magazine commits a CLASS 1 misdemeanor.\nSec. 9, 18-12-102(1) (struck words checked on page image): (1) As used in this section, the term \"dangerous weapon\" means a firearm silencer, machine gun, RAPID-FIRE DEVICE, short shotgun, or short rifle.",
